  "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=2X-3$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-9$ | $-5$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $7$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-9$ | $-5$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $P(Y=-1)=0.25.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
